      "candidate": "**Repaired scraper configuration (JSON)**  \n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"gpu-price\",\n  \"schema\": \"gpu-price-schema-v1\",\n  \"start_url\": \"https://example.test/gpu-1\",\n  \"extractions\": {\n    \"product_id\": {\n      \"from\": \"url\",\n      \"regex\": \"([^/]+)$\"\n    },\n    \"title\": {\n      \"selector\": \"h1.product-title,h1.title\",\n      \"attribute\": \"text\"\n    },\n    \"price\": {\n      \"selector\": [\n        \"span.price\",\n        \"span.price-value\",\n        \"div[data-price]\"\n      ],\n      \"attribute\": \"text\",\n      \"transform\": [\n        { \"regex\": \"\\\\$\\\\s*\", \"replace\": \"\" },\n        { \"type\": \"float\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"availability\": {\n      \"selector\": \"div.availability,span.stock-status\",\n      \"attribute\": \"text\",\n      \"map\": {\n        \"In Stock\": \"in_stock\",\n        \"Out of Stock\": \"out_of_stock\",\n        \"Pre\u2011order\": \"preorder\",\n        \"Available soon\": \"preorder\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"rating\": {\n      \"selector\": [\n        \"div.rating[data-rating]\",\n        \"div.rating span.value\",\n        \"span.star-rating\"\n      ],\n      \"attribute\": \"data-rating, text\",\n      \"transform\": { \"type\": \"float\" }\n    },\n    \"url\": {\n      \"selector\": \"link[rel=canonical], a[rel=canonical]\",\n      \"attribute\": \"href\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Explanation**\n\n* Added **fallback selectors** for every field to cover the page\u2011markup changes that triggered controlled mutation *M006* (e.g., price element changed class, rating switched from data attribute to text).  \n* Used a **regex extractor** on the URL to reliably pull `product_id`.  \n* Normalised price text (removed `$`/whitespace) and cast to float.  \n* Mapped human\u2011readable availability strings to machine\u2011readable tokens.  \n* Included a second capture for `rating` that reads from either a data attribute or visible text, ensuring extraction succeeds even if the site outputs rating differently.  \n\nThese changes restore the correct extraction of all fields while keeping the expected schema intact."
